# Docker build context filter. Unlike .gitignore, a pattern here matches from the context root only,
# so every rule that must apply at any depth is spelled with **/. This is the second line of defence
# behind .railwayignore: even a file that got uploaded never reaches an image layer.

# Secrets: every .env file anywhere; only the committed template is allowed through.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.vite

# Local runtime state, tooling and deploy metadata the image does not need.
data
.claude
.railway
**/*.log
**/*.local
**/.DS_Store
